      "content": "i see. so you think the majority's approach is the only way to avoid \"judicial legislation,\" but doesn't that ignore the precedents that were built on those privacy rights for decades? if the dissent is basically arguing that the Court has a responsibility to protect fundamental liberties even if they aren't explicitly in the text, isn't that a legitimate philosophical stance on how law should work, rather than just being \"wrong\"?",
